---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../../site.config.mjs';
const n = site.name;
---
<Base title={`About ${n}`}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-heading">About {n}</h1>
    <p>
      {n} is a personal archive of research papers by {site.author}. It follows the conventions of preprint servers
      (identifiers, versions, abstract pages, listings), but it hosts only the author's own work and has no submission
      or moderation process. Materials on this site are not peer-reviewed. {n} is not affiliated with arXiv or Cornell
      University.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ai">AI assistance and checking</h2>
    <p>
      The papers here are written through <em>vibe research</em>: the questions, the key ideas and the final judgement
      are the author's, and much of the exploration, computation and drafting is done with AI systems. Where the author
      has recorded it, the abstract page lists:
    </p>
    <dl class="defs">
      <dt>AI tools</dt><dd>the agent systems and models used.</dd>
      <dt>Author's role</dt><dd>what the author contributed directly.</dd>
      <dt>Checking</dt>
      <dd>
        how the results were checked: by AI (for example independent AI review of the manuscript or of the
        derivations, which is not formal verification), by the author by hand, and in a proof assistant such as Lean.
        Each can be stated as done, partly done or not done; anything not mentioned has not been stated.
      </dd>
      <dt>Materials</dt><dd>code, data or transcripts that support the paper.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>These statements are the author's own. Readers should check every claim independently before relying on it.</p>

    <h2 id="identifiers">Identifiers and versions</h2>
    <p>
      Every paper has a permanent identifier <code>{n}:YYMM.NNNN</code>. YYMM is the year and month of the first version
      (UTC) and NNNN is its order within that month. A specific version is cited as <code>{n}:YYMM.NNNNvN</code>; the
      identifier without a version always refers to the latest version.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Abstract page: <code>/abs/YYMM.NNNN/</code>, or <code>/abs/YYMM.NNNNvN/</code> for version N</li>
      <li>PDF: <code>/pdf/YYMM.NNNN.pdf</code>, or <code>/pdf/YYMM.NNNNvN.pdf</code> for version N</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These addresses do not change. A withdrawn paper is removed from the listings, the feed and search engines; its identifier and abstract page stay, with a withdrawal notice, so existing links still work.</p>

    <h2 id="integrity">Checksums</h2>
    <p>
      A posted PDF is never replaced; every change is posted as a new version. The submission history on each abstract
      page lists the SHA-256 checksum of every version. The site is built from a
      <a href={site.repoUrl}>public Git repository</a> whose commit history is an independent record of when each
      version was added, and the build fails if a stored PDF no longer matches its recorded checksum.
    </p>
    <p>To check a downloaded PDF, compute its checksum and compare it with the one on the abstract page:</p>
    <pre class="code">shasum -a 256 2611.0001v1.pdf              # macOS, Linux
certutil -hashfile 2611.0001v1.pdf SHA256  # Windows</pre>

    <h2 id="citing">Citing</h2>
    <p>
      Cite a paper as <code>{n}:YYMM.NNNN</code> together with its URL, adding <code>vN</code> to refer to a specific
      version. Each abstract page has a BibTeX entry under <em>Export BibTeX Citation</em>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="feed">Feed</h2>
    <p>New papers and new versions appear in the <a href="/feed.xml">Atom feed</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
